      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-22_WidnesExaminer_art0026" n="art0026">
        <head>SPOKEN AT WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>SPOKEN AT WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>A reporter of the Warrington "Examiner " recently had a conversation with Mr.M. Shaughnessy,living at 3, Milner-atreet, Warrington, and employed in the town at the large works of the St. Helena Cable Company, Ltd.. Mr. Shaughnessy is a sturdily-built man of medium heigb, with hair just . beginning to be tinged</p>
        <p>[From a Photo,] with grey, who has a record of thirty-one years' service in the army behind him. Mr. Shaughnessy has served in India, and there he con- tracted slow fever. Be also fought through the Zulu war in South Africa, and was there striken down with the dreaded enteric fever. " I was laid up four months there," said be, "and two months more at Netley Hospital when I came home. I blame my illness fi.r the horrible pains I have suffered since. The doctors told ma it was acute indigestion and I spasms and that I must be very careful." "I have tried all kinds of medicine and spent pounds, but until recently I dare not eat meat or drink tea, without these dreadful pains coming on. About two months age I read about the cures effectzd by Dr Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People and immediately got a box from the company in London. The pills did me good at once, and I have taken them ever since. Just before I began to take them I had a seizure, which came on like lightning, at the office here, and they thought I was going to die on the spot. But now I feel ever so much better,and can even take a little meat and potatoes. The pills are a wonder and no mistake. My wife has been taking them for indigestion lately, and they have done her good too."</p>
        <p>THE ONE It 'MEDIC FOR MANY DiazAsEs.---Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People enrich and purify the blood and strengthen the nervous system, so curing many forms of disease such as Anemia, "Decline," Consumption, Eczema, indigestion, Palpitati on of the Heart, Rheumatism, St. Vitus' Dance, Sciatica and Paralysis, nervous disorders in men, and ailments from which only women sutler. They are not purgative, and contain no ingredient that could harm the most delicate, They are sold by chemists everywhere, but should only be ac- cepted in boxes bearing the full name, Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People (seven words) on the wrapper; sent also, post froe,by Dr. Williams' Medicine Company, Holborn Viaduct, London, E.C., at 2s. 9d. a box, or six boxes for 13s. 9d.</p>
