        <p>are for Men, Women, and Children : for Old and Young: for Rich and Poor. They are not a Purgative and cannot harm the most delicate:</p>
        <p>SPOKEN IN LANCASHIRE.</p>
        <p>SPOKEN AT STOCKPORT.</p>
        <p>IMrs. Johnstone, of 17, Higher Croft, Barten-on-Irwell, 30 years of age, made the following statement to a reporter of the " Eccles Advertiser" :—" When I left the I hospital, where I had been for a long time, I was so ill I had to go upstairs on my hands and knees. The doctors said :medicine would do roe no good whatever. I bad had typhoid fever and internal inflammation, which left me in a very weak state, and I couldn't eat anything. A friend gave me some Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale I People. Before I had taken half a box I could get up at half-past five and eat a hearty breakfast with my husband, and I've t,ever gone off my eating since." .. were you very ill ? "—" Well, 1 gave myself Up</p>
        <p>A repor:er of the Cheshire" Daiiy Echo" was told tie following experience ty Charles Frederick Heywood. 29, years ef age, of Heaton-Nord., StoArport. About six months ago I found myself getting very thin. My appetite was entirely gone ; and what litAkt did eat came back again. I was troubled with a coy&amp; and my chest felt quite hollow. I bad to throw up twir work. I had to give up my home and come and live wft my sister. I went to see a doctor, and he told me one off my lungs was affected. Re advised me to take code:Veer oil, and to get out into the country. I tried the cod-Liver oil,but it would not stay on my stomaeb,and I continued to get worse. My cheeks sunk in, and I Lecame a mere skeleton. I made up my mind that I was gang to die. "And what has effected this wonderful change ?" asked the interviewer.</p>
        <p>Mrs. Heywood, bearing the quettion,-answered fait bee son. "You see," she said, "on the advice of aMead I got him a box of Dr. Williams Pik Pills for Pale PeoplP. My friend told me she had taken then herself, and now felt a different person altogether. liar lad took one or two boxes, and began Co improve. Hs then went to stay at Darley, in Shropshire*, ior two go</p>
        <p>[From a photo.] when I came out of the hospital, and the doctor said he would give me no more medicine. Of coarse you under- stand I was cured of fever in the hospital, but it was the weakness which remained. I used to be so dizzy that I couldh't walk across the floor without sitting down to rest ; I had to have my bed downstairs as I was unable to go up. I got worse and worse and as thin as a lath. I used to go hot and cold, and have cald sweats at the back of my bead, and I had awfully cold feet. I felt batter after the first half box. I've bad just five boxes altogether. " I don't take the pills regularly now, but only when I have a sinking feeling. I got them on the Saturday. and I was out of bed on the Thursday, and when the doctor came I was washing up, and I bad nut been out of bed for six weeks before."</p>
        <p>. CFUBLES _ _ATWOOD. [From a photo three months, and I cent bun Dr Williams' Pink Ping every week. •Yes, continued Mr Hermon&amp; "it is quite right, owe my life to Dr Williams' Pink Pills. After • few boxes I began to be able to eat something, and also to put on flesh. I can eat ancthiv.; now, and I feel better than ever I did in my life."</p>
