      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-22_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>20TH CENTURY.</head>
        <p>THE 20TH CENTURY.</p>
        <p>Do you know that it has often hr. 'n said that great events batmen at the end and at the berzinning of r. Century ? No doubt we shall have the usual prophets forecasting the probabilities of all sorts of startling occurrences to mark the commencement of the 20th Century, but there is no one bold enough to pre iict that there will be less of pain and suffering, less of human misery and disease in the World. The lot of huma.a kind is to suffer, and the greatest benefactor is he who does something to mitigate pain and affliction. "Never Fronheay till you know" is a wise sayinz, and we adept this maxim when we say that Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is destined to occupy a greatly extended sphere of usefulness in the new Century. It has been proved by thousands of sufferers to be the one safe and certain remedy for all Nervous Disorders, Low Spirits, Depres sion. Liver Complaints, Indigestion, and Genera Weakness.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-22_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>FEDERATION.</head>
        <p>FEDERATION.</p>
        <p>The welding ofi different communities for the common good is a grand idea, that is now seen in prozreas at the antipodes. This lathe kind of development in civilisation that makes Great Britain, hand-in-hand with Greater Britain, shine out as a jewel among the Nations of the World. Just as we witness in the world of Science, amid the humanising agencies for the amelioration of sickness and suffering. Note the comprehensive federation of Nature's helps and aids in Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. Here we have'Sarsaparilla," Gentian, Burdock, Lavender, Dandelion, Saffron, and Quinine all brought together, and each for those particular proper iee wanted to make perfect the requirements for remedying human suffering arising from Liver Disordere, Stomach Troubles, Indigestion, Weak Netrves. Pear -Blood, and Bodily Weakness from all Causes. Gwilvro Evans' Quinine Bitters is wanted by you—Fathers, Mothers, and Child- ren ; for there is no condition of life where a tonic is not required at some time, and this is Nature's own tonic, which meets all the demands of the human system. After attacks of Fever and Influenza, it re- coups the congtitation with vital energy. See that the name " Gwilym Evans" is on tho label, stamp, and bottle, then you are sure there is no mistake. At all Chemists and Stores, in bottles 2s 9d and 49 ed. A case of throe 4s 64 bottles for 124 64, or will be sent carriage free by the Solo Proprietors—The Quinine Bitters Manu- facturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-02-22_WidnesExaminer_art0063" n="art0063">
        <head>BEFORE the MAGISTRATES</head>
        <p>BEFORE the MAGISTRATES</p>
        <p>AN UNCONTI2,LLABLE BOY. A boy named Henry Millman, residing in Price-street, appeared bPf ore the Warrington magistrates on Satur- day on the charge of stealing a silver lever watch, value 30s, the property of hie father, JAMP9 Millman, at 9 o'clock the previous morning.--The Chief Constahla said the prisener's father was a labourer and was employed • Whitecross works. On Friday morning he went to work leaving the watch in the bedronm. Later on it was missed by the housekeeper from its accustomed pia en and information was given to the police. Inquiries • made and it was found that the boy bad pawned the watch for 5,: He had spent 31 in a football end other luxuries and when apprehended he had the vernaining 25 in his possession. Prisoner appeared to be a had boy and had become uncontrollable.—The magis- tintes ordered the boy to receive ten strokes of the birch Tod.</p>
      </div>
