        <p>Mrs Hrnest Crosfield hand-embroidered dress Mrs Robert Brassev. Indian silver bowl The Misses Okell, silver entree dishes Mr and Mrs 'Fere B Davies. silver candlesticks Mr Leonard G Davies, silver candlesticks Mr and Mrs 111 Gaskell Davies, dessert knives and forks Mrs James Sedley Davies, antique silver cream jug Mr and Mrs Richard Brassey, silver cake basket The in-door and out-door servants at Hemp Gill, two silver inuffineers Mr and Mrs Charles Reynolds,engravings" The Mortgage,' by Dendev Sadler, and "A Regal Gift,"by Drummond Mr and Mrs George Dakin, silver breakfast dish Dr and Mrs Steele, silver dessert dishes Mr Gerard Steele, silver mustard pot Mrs Broadbent, teacloth Mrs T Fanny Evans, silver-mounted scent bottle Mr and Mrs Algernon Pilkington, silver bon-bon dishes The Misses Crosiield. teacloth and duchesse cover Dr and Mrs Burton, silver egg stand Mrs Speakman brocaded satin cushion Mr and Mrs William Hutchins, copper fire [creel Miss Sylvia Broadbent, handkerchief satobet airs Deamont, embroidered tablecloth Mr Matt Steele. junior, silver tea caddy Mrs George Weave (Prodsham), antique lustre cream jugs Dr and Mrs Weaver, silver fruit spoons Mr Tinsley (Daresbury Hall), silver card ease Mrs Henry Reynolds, brocaded silk cushion Miss Pattie SI haw, letter weights The indoor and outdoor servants at Reaconhurst, silver salts</p>
