        <p>attack, and Birrell dropped a good goal. The visitors played up vigorously, taut the Widnes forwards respon- ded and carried play to the Rochdale line. Lally obtained from the scrummage and drooped a grand goal. Rigg responded, and Wightelan put in a splendid run, Batey just saving. Result :—Widnes, one goal and two tries (eight points) ; Rochdale Hsrners. one goal (two points). Runcorn v. St. Helens. At Runcorn, before 1,000 spectators. The ground was vary slippery. From the start Runcorn asserted their superiority. Jolley kicked a goal from a mark. The Runcorn backs passed several times in splendid style, and eventually alclever comb'ne ended in Nickson scor- ing a try. Jolley failed at goal, and then St Helens pressed, but could not score. Half-time score s—Run- corn, one goal and one try ;St Helens, nothing. On recommencing St Helens played with a dash that soon put them on the aggressive. Walker and Messenger retrieved the lost ground somewhat, but shortly after Houghton kicked dead. 8 Walker and W Houghton .then passed beautifully, Foulkes saving. Doherty and Appleton tried passing, but failed to get past the home three-quarters. Whiteley, of Sc. Helens, had to retire, and was attended by Dr. M'Lonnan for injuries to the back. Thus weakened, St Helens did little else but play on the defensive. Results :—Runcorn, one goal and one try (five points) ; St. Helens, nil. SOUTH-WEST LANCASHIRE AND BORDER TOWNS CUP. Semi-Final. Swinton V. Leigh. This match was played at Swinton on Tuesday after- , noon. Half-time :—No score. OR resuming, the game ' was stubbornly and evenly contested, and in the end Leigh won a hard-tough: game by four points to nil. The final no w lies between Loigh and Warrington, YORKSHIRE SENIOR COMPETITION -- Tuesday's Matches. Leeds Parish Church v. Bramley. This game was decided at Leeds on Tuesday. Results —A pointless draw. Huddersfield v. Hunslet. Played on Tuesday. Result :—lluddersifield,, three tries (nine points) ; Hunalet, nil. Bradford v. Batley. At Park Avenue, Bradford, on Tuesday. Result : Bradford, four goals one try (eleven points) ; Batley, one goal (two points). Halifax v. Manningham. This match took place at Halifax on Tuesday, Result . —Halifax, ope goal three tries (eleven points) ; Man ningham, one goal (two points).</p>
